 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "And, as a king mine hour,\nI will speak to thee alone in power.\nMy country's glory is thy name alone\nAs the bramble of our\nInfluenced time and cast away\nBy the iron hours whose hands decay\nThe lifeless growth that grows withering and\nSwings its black leaves through space. From our\nHands are we made: not mortal hands,\nNot made by man, but only\nMade by God for us who sit here alone\nWatching the wild sea die out again",
